export anchor CommandFirstStyle:
    number: 176
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Command first
    idea: A sparse home built around one large search and command field with keyboard hints, followed by a hairline strip of four figures and quiet unboxed lists, graphite text with a single violet accent.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #fbfbfc, the near-white page
        paper: #ffffff, the command field, buttons and fields
        ink: #22242a, graphite text
        muted: #5c5f69, labels, meta, times and day letters
        hair: #e4e5ea, hairline rules under rows and around the figure strip
        violet: #5b3fd1, the primary button, links, progress, this week bars and focus
        violetSoft: #efebfc, the focus halo of the command field and the initials disc
        keycap: #f1f1f4, keyboard hint caps and the current nav pill
        keycapLine: #d3d4dc, keycap borders
        keycapInk: #3b3e47, keycap letters
        lastWeek: #8a8d98, dashed outlines of last week bars
        ok: #1f7a4d, On track text and check circle
        risk: #925400, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #b3261e, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        Two stacks. Text uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial at 15px and 1.55. Keycaps and sheet notes use ui-monospace, SF
        Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 12px. The greeting is 34px
        at 600 with minus 0.02em tracking, the command input 17px, figures
        26px at 600 with tabular numbers, list headings 13px at 600 in muted
        sentence case, rows 15px and meta 13px.
    layout:
        A slim top line in a 1120px container with a small violet diamond
        and the wordmark, the six nav items as quiet text pills with Home in
        a grey pill, and a bell and Mara Okafor at right. Then a centred
        720px hero with lots of air above it, the date in muted text, a 34px
        greeting, a red overdue line with a Show them link, and the command
        field, 60px tall with a 14px radius, a search icon, the placeholder
        Search or type a command, and Ctrl K keycaps at the right end. Under
        it three centred action buttons each carry a keycap, a violet New
        project with N, Overdue tasks with G O and Log time with T. Next a
        full-width strip of four figures between hairlines, each a number
        followed by a lowercase label on one line. Below sit two unboxed
        lists side by side, Projects at three fifths and Recent activity at
        two fifths, each under a muted heading and hairline. Project rows
        show name over category, a thin violet progress line with percent,
        due date and status. Activity rows show the sentence and the time at
        right. The chart runs full width beneath, airy bars with dashed
        outlines last week and violet this week. A footer hint reads Press ?
        for all keyboard shortcuts. Below 960px the lists stack, below 760px
        figures go two by two and keycaps leave the field.
    spacing: An 8px unit with generous gaps. 72px above the hero, 32px from greeting to field, 40px between sections, 56px between the two lists, 11px row padding.
    density: Sparse at the top, medium in the lists. One focal control and little chrome.
    corners: Soft. 14px on the command field, 8px on buttons and fields, 5px keycaps, 4px bar tops, round initials.
    borders: Hairlines only, under rows and around the figure strip. No cards. The command field has a 1px grey edge.
    shadows: One soft violet-tinted shadow under the command field. Nothing else is raised.
    icons:
        Thin line icons at 1.5px stroke, 18px, 22px in the field. Status
        icons use 2px stroke, a check circle for On track, a triangle for At
        risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
        with the word. Keycaps carry shortcuts.
    focus: A 2px white gap then a 2px violet ring as a box shadow, and the command field gains a violet edge and a soft violet halo.
    tone: Calm and terse with lowercase figure labels such as tasks due this week, and command verbs such as Show them and Log time.
